"""Repair seven previously missing Phase 5 readings with scoped M4 bridges."""
import argparse
from html import escape
from build_catalog import SITE
from build_reading_links import integrate
from build_course import navigation

PAGES={
'06-double-dqn.html':('Double DQN','''<p>Vanilla DQN uses r+γ max Qtarget(s′,a). Double DQN separates action selection from evaluation: online selects the largest legal estimate, target supplies its value. Target computation is detached and true termination has no continuation.</p><pre><code>selected = online_next.masked_fill(~legal, -torch.inf).argmax(1)
continuation = target_next.gather(1, selected[:, None]).squeeze(1)
target = reward + gamma * continuation</code></pre><p>Apply this only to nonterminal rows; terminal rows may have no legal successor. For online [5,4,100], target [1,7,99] and mask [true,true,false], reward 1 and γ=.5 give Double target 1.5, versus vanilla 4.5. Noisy maximization can produce upward bias; the method mitigates a source of bias without a universal performance guarantee.</p><p><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1509.06461">Primary Double DQN paper</a></p>''','p5-double-dueling'),
'07-prioritized-experience-replay.html':('Prioritized experience replay','<p>Retain raw priority p=|TD error|+ε. The sampling mass is p^α, so probabilities normalize those masses. α=0 recovers uniform replay. Insert a new item with the maximum retained raw priority, or 1 for an empty buffer. Applying α before storage and again at sampling is a different, erroneous exponent.</p><p>Importance weights are (N P(i))^(−β). The lab normalizes by the maximum over all retained entries; this convention differs from minibatch-only normalization. β=0 removes correction. Use mean(weight × per-item squared error), with weights detached. For [1,4,9], α=.5, β=1: probabilities [1/6,1/3,1/2], weights [1,.5,1/3].</p><p>Sampling is with replacement. Uniform replay does not make rare retained entries impossible to sample; PER changes allocation and introduces a correction problem.</p><p><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1511.05952">Primary PER paper</a></p>','p5-per'),
'08-reward-scale-trap.html':('The reward-scale trap','<p>Reward magnitudes affect target magnitudes, losses and gradients. If predictions and targets both scale by c, squared loss scales by c². A fixed optimizer step or clipping threshold therefore need not behave equivalently after scaling.</p><p>Large or flat loss alone does not identify a reward-scale bug. Inspect finite tensors, selected-action shapes, terminal flags, detached targets, reward ranges and gradient norms first. Compare returns on the original reward scale. Report any normalization and undo it for comparisons that require original units.</p><p>Exercise: compute MSE for errors [1,−2], then [10,−20]. The losses are 2.5 and 250. Explain why that calculation does not predict an agent’s return.</p>','p5-network'),
'09-build-it-yourself.html':('Build it yourself','<p>Use four small stages rather than one large agent. First implement tensor prediction, mean loss and an SGD update against fixed labels. Next implement FIFO replay and a detached, independently stored target. Then add online selection with target evaluation and a centered dueling head. Finally implement raw priorities and fixed importance weights.</p><p>Run each downloaded pack’s checks before integrating it. The stability pack also provides a small chain-training CLI and three equal-budget ablations. Run multiple seeds; do not require one variant to win. The supervised fit is a warm-up, not DQN.</p><p>Help remains opt-in in each lab; predictions and explanations are yours.</p>','p5-stability'),
'10-this-project-formalized.html':('This project, formalized','<p>Transfer the mechanisms through contracts. State features form an input batch (B,D); the value network returns (B,A); a chosen action gathers one prediction per transition. Replay stores state, action, reward, next state, true termination and truncation separately. Only true termination removes a continuing-task bootstrap.</p><p>Legal masks must match the action space and enter exploration and successor selection. Specify whether target synchronization counts environment steps or optimizer updates. The teaching chain uses hard copies every eight optimizer updates; a project may instead specify soft updates. These are different schedules.</p><p>Before following your Phase 5 implementation plan, map its feature/action sizes, reward units, replay capacity, target schedule and raw priority convention to these contracts. The small lab hyperparameters are teaching choices, not recommended production settings.</p>','p5-double-dueling'),
'11-code-walkthrough.html':('Code walkthrough','<p>This walkthrough refers to the supplied standalone exercise files, which you can inspect and run now. It does not assume a production DQN agent has already been implemented.</p><ol><li>README.md defines functions, shapes and run commands.</li><li>exercise_common.py defines validation helpers and the small witness CLI.</li><li>starter.py is your implementation surface; broken.py contains deliberate defects.</li><li>checks.py imports your chosen candidate and verifies independent numerical examples and invariants without importing the solution.</li><li>In the network pack, compare.py fits fixed labels and reports held-out error. In stability, it collects chain transitions, samples replay, computes detached targets, updates selected predictions, then synchronizes on the optimizer schedule.</li></ol><p>Optional solution.py is reference help. Inspect it only when you request it. Trace one transition through the learner before scaling up.</p>','p5-stability'),
'12-glossary.html':('Glossary','<dl><dt>Forward pass</dt><dd>Compute outputs from inputs and parameters.</dd><dt>Scalar loss</dt><dd>One objective differentiated by autograd.</dd><dt>Replay</dt><dd>Resample retained transitions; FIFO controls retention, not sampling order.</dd><dt>Target snapshot</dt><dd>Independent parameter storage with a specified refresh schedule.</dd><dt>Detachment</dt><dd>Prevent a computation from contributing gradients.</dd><dt>Double DQN</dt><dd>Online selects the successor action; target evaluates it.</dd><dt>Dueling</dt><dd>Value plus row-centered advantages represent action values.</dd><dt>Raw priority</dt><dd>Positive error-derived quantity before exponentiation.</dd><dt>Importance weight</dt><dd>Correction for changed sampling probabilities, fixed during differentiation.</dd><dt>Ablation</dt><dd>Remove a mechanism under stated budgets and conditions; not a correctness proof.</dd></dl>','p5-per')}

def outputs():
    folder=SITE/'phase-5-dqn-prerequisites'
    result={}
    for filename,(title,body,lab) in PAGES.items():
        nav=navigation('phase-5-dqn-prerequisites/'+filename)
        result[folder/filename]=f'''<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>{escape(title)} — Phase 5</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/style.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../assets/course.css"><script type="module" src="../assets/course-navigation.js"></script></head><body><a href="#main">Skip to reading</a><div class="course-reference">{nav}<main id="main"><div class="doc"><p class="eyebrow">Phase 5 · M4 concept bridge</p><h1>{escape(title)}</h1>{body}<p><a href="../labs/phase-5/{lab}.html">Learn by doing: {lab}</a> · <a href="index.html">Phase 5 topic reference</a></p></div></main></div></body></html>
'''
    return {path:integrate(path,source) for path,source in result.items()}

if __name__=='__main__':
    p=argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__);p.add_argument('--write',action='store_true');a=p.parse_args()
    for path,source in outputs().items():
        if a.write:path.write_text(source,encoding='utf-8')
        elif not path.exists() or path.read_text(encoding='utf-8')!=source:raise SystemExit(f'Stale M4 reading: {path}')
    print('Seven Phase 5 reading bridges '+('generated.' if a.write else 'are current.'))
